# .cursorrules — mini-solana-turbine

## PROJECT OVERVIEW
`mini-solana-turbine` is a high-performance, low-latency block propagation and shred ingestion engine in Rust. It mimics the core network pipeline of a Solana validator, leveraging Linux `io_uring` for UDP kernel bypass, SIMD-accelerated Reed-Solomon erasure coding, and lock-free data structures.

---

## 1. TECHNICAL STACK & CONSTRAINTS

- **Language & Standard:** Rust (2021 edition or newer).
- **Crate layout:** un solo crate (no workspace). Seguir el árbol de la sección 3.
- **Core Dependencies:**
  - `tokio` & `tokio-uring` (Linux `io_uring` async UDP sockets)
  - `reed-solomon-simd` (AVX2 / SIMD-accelerated erasure coding)
  - `crossbeam-epoch` / `dashmap` / `crossbeam-channel` (lock-free; no `Bytes` para payloads)
  - `thiserror` (únicos errores de crate y binario; **no** `anyhow`)
  - `criterion` (benchmarks)
- **Target OS:** Linux x86_64 (Kernel 6.8+).
- **Forbidden Patterns:**
  - Cero allocs de heap en hot paths (no `Vec`/`Box`/`String`/`Bytes` para paquetes).
  - No `unwrap()` or `expect()` in production modules.
  - Payloads: slices sobre **arenas estáticas** de tamaño fijo. No clonar `Vec<u8>`.
- **Documentación:** proyecto de aprendizaje. Toda función lleva `///` con Purpose, Inputs y Returns.
- **`unsafe`:** permitido solo acotado, con comentario `SAFETY:` que justifique invariantes.
- **Fases:** implementar según `FASES.md`; no saltar de fase sin autorización.

---

## 2. RUST CODING CONVENTIONS & ARCHITECTURE

- **Memory Layout:** Wire protocol structs (`ShredHeader`, `DataShred`, `CodeShred`) must be declared with `#[repr(C)]` or `#[repr(packed)]` to guarantee binary compatibility without intermediate serialization layers.
- **Inlining:** Annotate all hot-path functions (shred parsing, XOR operations, header validation) with `#[inline(always)]`.
- **Concurrency:** Prefer atomics (`AtomicU64`, `AtomicBool`) and lock-free queues (`crossbeam-channel`) over heavy sync primitives (`Mutex`, `RwLock`).
- **Error Handling:** Use custom error enums via `thiserror`. Propagate errors explicitly using `?`.

---

## 3. PROJECT DIRECTORY STRUCTURE

```text
mini-solana-turbine/
├── Cargo.toml
├── FASES.md
├── .gitignore
├── .cursorrules
├── rust.cursorrules
├── src/
│   ├── lib.rs
│   ├── main.rs
│   ├── shred.rs            # Binary Shred layouts (Data vs Code) & Zero-Copy parsing
│   ├── ingress/
│   │   ├── mod.rs
│   │   └── uring_udp.rs    # io_uring UDP ring buffer receiver
│   ├── fec/
│   │   ├── mod.rs
│   │   └── reed_solomon.rs # SIMD Erasure Coding decoder & reconstruction
│   └── turbine/
│       ├── mod.rs
│       └── tree.rs         # Stake-weighted fanout tree calculation & routing
└── benches/
    └── shred_throughput.rs # Latency & Gbps throughput benchmarks
